<title>USA: Fed stayed out of open market, Tuesday add seen.</title>
<headline>Fed stayed out of open market, Tuesday add seen.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve, as expecetd, stayed out of the open market Friday, players said.</p>
<p>Analysts said Thursday's execution of five-day fixed system repurchase agreements was sufficient to take care of the add need through the Veterans Day holiday on Monday.</p>
<p>But, with a projected $6.5 billion average daily add need seen for the surrent reseerve period, the Fed will have to add reserves again on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Steven Scheer, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867</p>
